[6e] E2 stationary content with the eps profile e(s) = (s^2 + eps^2)/(s^2 + eps) (R13-6 [2], delta = sqrt(eps)), near cone, W = 1
     Var_E2(g) = (1/4pi) int_{-S}^{S} e(s) ds / sqrt(s^2 + g^2)  (s = W^2 - w^2 ~ 2(W - w)); secular part = coefficient of ln(1/g)
     eps=1e-02: Var(g=1e-6..1e-9) = 0.386678, 0.390343, 0.394008, 0.397672; d Var/d ln(1/g) = 1.592e-03 (eps/2pi = 1.592e-03)
       remainder after eps ln(eps/g)/2pi: 0.37202, 0.37202, 0.37202, 0.37202  (forced part ~ ln(1/eps)/(4pi) = 0.36647)
     eps=1e-03: Var(g=1e-6..1e-9) = 0.551541, 0.551907, 0.552274, 0.552640; d Var/d ln(1/g) = 1.592e-04 (eps/2pi = 1.592e-04)
       remainder after eps ln(eps/g)/2pi: 0.55044, 0.55044, 0.55044, 0.55044  (forced part ~ ln(1/eps)/(4pi) = 0.54970)
     => secular slope eps/(2pi) per ln(1/g), the same coefficient as E1 per ln T; the constant equals the forced part ln(1/eps)/(4pi) to O(eps ln eps), so whether eps sits inside the log is a convention at that order; the forced part is the same in E1 and E2. subtraction: none

